Current architecture

The current color pipeline is:

Wallpaper
    ↓
Matugen
    ↓
~/.config/quickshell/Theme/colors.json
    ↓
~/.config/quickshell/Theme/Colors.qml
    ↓
Quickshell UI


This architecture should be preserved.

Do NOT replace Matugen unless there is a compelling technical reason. Matugen already provides the Material-style wallpaper palette that I want.

Important color decision

My Matugen template intentionally uses the opposite light/dark palette in some cases.

This is NOT an accidental mistake.

The reason is that I want Quickshell windows, panels, cards, etc. to have enough contrast against the wallpaper.

For example, when running a dark desktop, I may intentionally use the lighter Material palette for shell surfaces so the UI remains visually separated from a dark wallpaper.

Do not automatically "fix" this by assuming:

dark mode = Matugen dark colors
light mode = Matugen light colors


The desired behavior is:

Wallpaper-derived colors
        ↓
Material palette
        ↓
Choose surface tones that provide good contrast with wallpaper


Eventually this should be made more deliberate, perhaps through Material contrast settings or a shell-level surface strategy, rather than simply swapping entire palettes.

